Exam content provenance
-----------------------
Exercise formats (reading, listening, writing, speaking) follow the publicly
documented structure of the Goethe-Zertifikat A1/A2 exams. Exam task types
are modelled on that structure; the sentences and answers inside them are
not.

The vocabulary is a different matter and is disclosed plainly: the word list
in js/data/words.js was built against the official Goethe-Zertifikat A1
"Start Deutsch 1" Wortliste published by the Goethe-Institut, and the A2 list
in js/data/words-a2.js was built the same way against the A2 vocabulary. The
selection of which words appear, and its grouping into categories, therefore
follows a Goethe-Institut publication. The German articles, English
translations, and example sentences attached to each word are original to
this project. The app states this itself in its vocabulary footer.

Because of that derivation, the CC BY-SA 4.0 grant in LICENSE-CONTENT covers
the original translations and example sentences but does not extend to the
vocabulary selection itself. This repository has no standing to license the
Goethe-Institut's list, and it does not grant commercial reuse of it. Anyone
who needs the underlying word list should obtain it from the Goethe-Institut
under their terms.

Everything else under js/data/ — dialogues, reading texts, form and speaking
prompts, warm-up questions, schedules — was written for this project. Much of
it, and the bulk of later A2/B1 copy, was drafted with AI assistance. This is
the maintainer's best understanding of provenance, not a guarantee: model-
assisted drafting can reproduce phrasing nobody intended to use. If you
believe something here reproduces or closely paraphrases a source it should
not, open an issue naming the file and the source; it will be rewritten,
credited, or removed promptly, with the correction visible in history.

Third-party components
----------------------
No third-party libraries, fonts, or datasets are bundled. The app is plain
HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with no build step and no runtime dependencies.

One third-party request is made at runtime: a cookieless page-view counter
(GoatCounter) is loaded from gc.zgo.at and reports to a self-hosted endpoint,
scoped to a single aggregate path. It sets no cookies, stores no personal
data, and performs no cross-site tracking. Fork authors who do not want it can
delete the script tag at the end of index.html — nothing depends on it.

All user state — flashcard progress, quiz scores, practice counts, schedule
checkmarks, self-intro fields — is held in localStorage on the user's own
device and never leaves the browser. The service worker cache is likewise
local. Only anonymous aggregate page views are transmitted.

